 {"id":"CF-015","title":"P5 — README says three environment variables but documents only two and the scripts expose two","status":"complete","priority":"P5","complexity":1,"reasoning":"README.md:73-74 says: Three environment variables and one harness are all it assumes, then exports only CRIER_URL and BUNKER_SERVER. Source inspection of the published scripts found those two relevant environment reads; the Hermes provider key is read from ~/.hermes/.env, not a third environment variable. docs/OPERATIONS.md:24,38,47-48,58 confirms BUNKER_SERVER and CRIER_URL are the documented variables and the provider key is configured out of band in ~/.hermes/.env. The fresh published-tree probe also ran the exact README commands: env -u BUNKER_SERVER bash scripts/bunker-server-install.sh --check -> rc=1 before checks; env -u CRIER_URL bash scripts/project-node.sh --check --project demo -> rc=1 with NODE: FAIL (3); bash tests/selftest.sh -> rc=0 SELFTEST: PASS. Fix: say Two environment variables and one harness, or enumerate a real third variable; keep the provider-key file requirement separate. ch:trace row=CF-015 spec=README.md#running-it-against-your-own-infrastructure wave=code-factory-readme-2026-10-29-22-35-38#readme test=tests/selftest.sh::selftest doc=README.md prompt=prompts/readme.md evidence=docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-29-22-35-38.md witness=path@origin:README.md verdict=none:open-finding commit=396f13387a050643898e37f06a6403e02954b07c memory=none:not-written","acceptance_criteria":"1. The README's environment-variable count matches the variables it documents and the source scripts actually consume. 2. The provider-key file requirement remains described as a file-based prerequisite, not silently counted as an environment variable. 3. From a fresh published archive, bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS. 4. The audit artifact docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-29-22-35-38.md remains committed and contains the exact pre-fix command/output evidence."