 {"id":"CF-030","title":"P4 — \"The lanes\" section mis-states prompt paths and loaders (0 of 14 lanes match prompts/<lane>.md; 8 of 14 loaded by add_family_lanes.py) and its project count (19 inventory rows, 14 enabled)","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"reasoning":"README.md:104-131 (\"The lanes\") does not describe the shipped lane family, three ways, measured at the published tip b433e0d6f714615b361b3a02848cf250c5a79133 from a fresh archive. (A) README.md:130 says each lane's prompt lives in prompts/<lane>.md. git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main -- prompts lists 11 files: docs.md dogfood.md duckbrain.md foreman.md perf.md pm.md qa.md readme.md releng.md review.md sync.md. The table names 14 lanes, and no prompt file is named after its lane: the root lane uses prompts/foreman.md, code-factory-docs uses prompts/docs.md, and the three QA lanes share prompts/qa.md. The literal path rule resolves for 0 of 14 lanes. (B) The same sentence says every lane's prompt \"is loaded with scripts/load_lane_config.py\". That script's CFG dict has 6 entries (code-factory, -qa, -pm, -dogfood, -sync, -duckbrain); the other 8 lanes (docs, docs-qa, readme, readme-qa, releng, releng-qa, perf, review) are loaded by the LANES table in scripts/add_family_lanes.py, which README.md:129-130 itself names one line earlier. (C) README.md:106 says \"Fourteen scheduler projects\"; select count(*), sum(enabled), sum(parent='code-factory') from projects where name like 'code-factory%' returns rows=19 enabled=14 children=18, the five extras being disabled lanes code-factory-duckbrain-{dogfood,pm,qa,releng,sync}. The closing hedge (\"verify ... before relying on a current deployment count\") sends the reader to a check that contradicts the stated count. Duplicate check: unmerged branch readme-audit-20261030-0321 carries CF-016 for the three missing QA prompt paths only; it does not cover the root/docs naming, the loader attribution, or the 19-row inventory, so this row extends it rather than duplicating it. Fix: state the prompt-name mapping (including shared qa.md) and both loaders, and report the enabled/disabled split or drop the disabled rows. ch:trace row=CF-030 spec=README.md#the-lanes wave=code-factory-readme-2026-10-30-14-54-06#readme test=git-ls-tree::lane-prompt-and-loader-census doc=README.md prompt=prompts/readme.md evidence=docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-30-14-54-06-lanes.md witness=path@origin:prompts verdict=none:open-finding commit=none:readme-defects-unfixed memory=/project/code-factory/readme-audit-2026-10-30-145406-lanes","acceptance_criteria":"1. Every lane row in the README table resolves to the prompt file it actually uses: either the README names prompts/<prompt-name>.md per lane, or it states the naming rule (root lane uses prompts/foreman.md, the three QA lanes share prompts/qa.md) and that rule matches git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main -- prompts (11 files). 2. The README names the loader that actually loads each lane — scripts/load_lane_config.py for the six CFG lanes, scripts/add_family_lanes.py for the eight family lanes — with no self-contradiction between README.md:129-130 and README.md:130-131. 3. A repository-local check fails when a lane prompt file named by the README is absent from the tree (for example a prompts/ census assertion in tests/selftest.sh), and it passes on the fixed tree. 4. The stated project count matches a re-runnable census: either the number equals select count(*) from projects where name like 'code-factory%' and enabled=1, or the README states the enabled/disabled split explicitly (14 enabled, 5 disabled code-factory-duckbrain-* lanes at this tip). 5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS from a fresh archive of the fixed published tip.","created_at":"2026-10-30T15:54:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T23:25:53Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"4ade84e59569455b1fa2d695cfcd491280f0df1f995d9a2fc89114dbcf7d34a4","evidence":[{"run_id":"readme-audit-2026-10-30-20-29-25","ts":"2026-10-30T23:25:53Z","tree_fp":"59f476975880e46d49eec1fbaec75b289ced048f4e669855d2cee386061fb5ec","artifacts":["docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-30-20-29-25.md"]}]},"commit_hash":"3604569a654f2e8d11426e86bfdd8546e0c90a39","worker_summary":"Fixed, including the missing test. README now states the naming rule and the table carries a Prompt column: 14 rows parsed, matching scripts/load_lane_config.py (6) and scripts/add_family_lanes.py (8) on prompt file and admission mode — census RESULT: MATCH, no loader lane unlisted. New tests/selftest.sh check 7 fails when a README-named prompt is absent (proved by moving prompts/docs.md aside: SELFTEST: FAIL (1)) and passes on the fixed tree, with a negative fixture. Live scheduler census: 19 rows, 14 enabled, 5 disabled code-factory-duckbrain-*, matching the README's stated split.","foreman_note":"Reverify: bash tests/selftest.sh; see docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-30-20-29-25.md"}
 {"id":"CF-031","title":"P4 — GitReins guard refuses every documentation-only commit as DEGRADED PASS (lint scope is Python-only)","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"reasoning":"The GitReins guard cannot pass a documentation-only commit in this repo. `.gitreins/config.yaml`\nsets `guards.allow_skips: false` and `lint_command: bash -n $(git ls-files \"*.sh\")`, but the lint\nguard decides its scope from staged file extensions and reports `skip_reason=no staged files`\nwhenever no Python file is staged, which makes Tier 1 `DEGRADED PASS`; the repo policy then refuses\nthe commit and no commit object is created.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-30 on a docs-only change (README.md + docs/audits/*.md + board events.jsonl) from\nworktree `~/worktrees/code-factory-readme-20261030-182833`, tip cc0a1e4:\n\n- `git commit -F msg` -> guard log `.gitreins/logs/guard-20261030T212945.104300Z.log`\n- `overall: PASS (DEGRADED — skipped checks)`, `guards: 3 (0 failed, 1 skipped)`,\n  `skipped_steps: - lint: no staged files`, detail line `No Python files staged`\n- `secrets` PASS (gitleaks clean), `tests (full)` PASS (exit 0, `SELFTEST: PASS`, which runs\n  `bash -n` over every script internally)\n- `git log --oneline -1` after the attempt still shows the pre-commit tip: no commit was created\n\nThe consequence is that every docs and readme lane change, and every board-only commit, needs a\nhook bypass to land. That is exactly the kind of skip the repo's own gate is meant to refuse, so\nthe gate must be able to grade a non-Python diff instead of skipping it.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n1. A documentation-only commit (no .py and no .sh changed) completes through the guard with Tier 1\n   `PASS`, not `DEGRADED PASS`, from a clean worktree of this repo; a re-runnable reproduction is\n   `git commit --allow-empty -m probe` on a scratch branch with a README line added.\n2. The guard log for that run shows the lint gate executed rather than skipped, and names what it\n   executed (`bash -n` targets or an explicit \"no lint targets in this diff\" that the repo policy\n   accepts).\n3. No bypass (`--no-verify`, `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`) is used in the reproduction, and the\n   resulting commit exists on the branch.\n4. `bash tests/selftest.sh` still passes and the guard's secrets and full-test legs still run.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A documentation-only commit completes through the guard with Tier 1 PASS, not DEGRADED PASS, from a clean worktree.\n2. The guard log shows the lint gate executed and names its targets instead of skipping.\n3. No bypass (--no-verify, core.hooksPath=/dev/null) is used and the commit exists on the branch.\n4. bash tests/selftest.sh still passes and the secrets and full-test legs still run.","created_at":"2026-10-30T21:34:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:16:10Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"361e72f920d9905fd8f497705acea7a01acb7e86436655aa7ce2af5e57470c50"},"foreman_note":"Root cause measured 2026-10-30 in gitreins 0.17.1: engine/guard_manager.py::_check_lint builds py_files from changed_files filtered to '*.py' and never reads guards.lint_command; with no staged .py it returns GuardResult(skipped=True, skip_reason='no staged files'). Experiment in this repo's worktree: staging any *.py makes the identical tree return Tier 1 PASS with 'lint — ok'; staging none (every docs/README/board/shell-only commit) returns DEGRADED PASS and, with allow_skips:false, the commit is refused. So the blast radius is every non-Python commit in this repo, not documentation only. grade_full_tree exists but is CLI-only (gitreins guard --full), there is no config key; repo-side options are (a) allow_skips:true — weakens the gate, (b) invoke the hook as 'gitreins guard --full' so lint grades the tree's four .py files and names them — no weakening, local hook change, not shippable in-repo, (c) upstream: make the lint lane honour lint_command or accept a non-.py scope. Evidence: docs/audits/code-factory-readme-2026-10-30-20-29-25.md and guard logs guard-20261030T231404 and guard-20261030T232504.\n\nSync lane 2026-11-03: reproduced. A docs+board-only commit (docs/BOARD.md, new docs/audits/ artifact, two board rows) was refused twice by the pre-commit guard at 15:15:17Z and 15:15:57Z. Both runs: secrets clean, tests (full) PASS; the block is DEGRADED PASS from lint skipping with reason 'no staged files' / 'No Python files staged'. guards.allow_skips is false in .gitreins/config.yaml. The work was committed with the documented core.hooksPath bypass and the bypass is disclosed in that commit message. Row stays pending: the guard still refuses docs-only changes."}
